# arc42

System design docs use the [arc42](https://arc42.org/) 12-section skeleton. The spine is `docs/arc42.md`.

Diagrams live in `docs/C4.md`. Decisions live in `adr/NNNN-slug.md`. Glossary is `CONTEXT.md`. Quality scenarios live in `docs/quality.md`.

Sections **point** at those files. Do not paste Mermaid or ADR bodies into the spine.

When the user asked for a system design, always write §1, §3, §5, §9, §12. Skip any other section with one line of why. Do not pad.

Terms come from `CONTEXT.md`. A hard-to-reverse choice is an ADR, not a paragraph in §4 or §9.

Writing or updating the spine: skill `system-design`.
